# Custody and physical holding establish protection duties, not shelter or speech actuality.
# ── Chapter 3 fidelity pins: "What You Are Owed" ─────────────────────────────
#
# The header also lists, for a reader checking them, the cases behind
# sections of other chapters; each pointer names its chapter.
#
# Chapter 21, "A way to be heard", is exercised across the named justice
# domains:
#   tests/pins/justice/access/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/assistance/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/hearing/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/survivor/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/restoration/claimant-Withdrawal/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/case-relief/without-actual-court-authority/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/general-invalidation/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/composition-review/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/enforcement/no-general-invalidation/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/enforcement/no-custodial-remedy-kind/expect.pins.nibli
# Field omission, domain, independence and counterfactual cases remain separate.
#
# Chapter 15's "Rights do not stop at arrival" uses these actual-constitution
# cases:
#   tests/pins/mobility/asylum/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/mobility/removal/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/mobility/nationality/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/mobility/external/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/mobility/boundaries/standing-rights-and-no-coercive-consequence/expect.pins.nibli
# These establish rights, duties and bounded compatibility, not operating
# borders, detention/removal authority, external truth or completed remedy.
#
# Chapter 15's "Conflicting versions stop the finding" rests on the same
# family's record-ambiguity sequence:
#   tests/pins/mobility/asylum/conflict-sequence/expect.pins.nibli
# The determination completes, an authorised writer then records a second
# constitutional version on the single-valued source-version scope, and the
# completion derives FALSE; the fixture pins that change. A measurement with
# the same fixture on 2026-09-16 also found the operator's duty to provide a
# fair determination TRUE before the second entry and FALSE after it, and
# `false`, `prisoner` and `lose` concluded for the person at no point.
# Nothing establishes that a determination was ever made, corrected or
# reached anybody.
#
# Chapter 11's shifted burden in a remedial proceeding, and the wall between
# statistics and a person's record, are exercised by these statistical cases:
#   tests/pins/statistics/pattern/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/statistics/pattern/defect-and-rights-sequence/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/statistics/data-wall/criminal-burden/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/statistics/data-wall/counterfactual-criminal-burden/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/statistics/data-wall/nonparticipation-is-not-a-penalty/expect.pins.nibli
# They establish no population finding or operated equality programme.
#
# Chapter 8, "What nobody has to ask permission for", rests on these
# actual-constitution knowledge cases:
#   tests/pins/knowledge/restriction/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/restriction/without-KnowledgeHarmEvidenceScope/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/restriction/without-KnowledgeNeutralityScope/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/restriction/kind-KnowledgeHarmKindScope-UnapprovedKnowledgeKind/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/restriction/actor-review/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/enforcement/without-authorization/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/enforcement/wrong-matter/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/restriction-does-not-travel-between-fields/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/restriction-defect-and-rights-sequence/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/residual-freedom-licenses-no-restriction/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/a-noted-belief-is-not-a-conclusion/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/concentration-finding-judges-no-content/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/request-and-certified-nonresponse/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/information/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/accessibility/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/autonomy/positive/expect.pins.nibli
# The per-scope omission, unauthorized-attester, stale, conflicting-value and
# counterfactual cases remain separate. They establish what must be shown before
# a restriction stands and what is owed while it has not been shown; they
# establish no publication, translation, answer or reader.
#
# Chapter 5, "When there is genuinely not enough", rests on these
# actual-constitution scarcity cases:
#   tests/pins/scarcity/finding/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/finding/without-ScarcityAlternativesScope/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/finding/without-ScarcityNotAFailureScope/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/finding/manager-review/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/allocation/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/allocation/without-ScarcityEqualShareScope/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/allocation/without-ScarcityUselessDivisionRefusalScope/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/allocation/without-authorization/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/shortfall/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/forbidden-Wealth/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/counterfactual-forbidden-wealth/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/false-scarcity-stops-the-allocation/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/finding-does-not-cover-another-resource/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/request-and-certified-nonresponse/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/forged-conclusions/expect.pins.nibli
# Every forbidden priority key and every refused ground has its own named case
# beside these; the per-scope omission, unauthorized-attester, stale and
# conflicting-value cases stay separate. They establish what must be true before
# scarcity may be acted on and what stays owed afterwards; they hold no stock,
# forecast no supply and prove no procurement, delivery or repair.
# Full interface and evidence limits:
#   book-1/appendix/contracts/scarcity-and-conflict-contract.md
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/03-what-you-are-owed.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # all substantive pins and formal contradiction checks
# Markdown consistency is reviewed separately; the pins do not certify prose.
#
# NOTE — one absence this file cannot hold as a query, and it is load-bearing.
# "Nothing in the rules reads the debt itself or turns it into something
# received" rests on nothing anywhere READING `owe`. The obligations family
# gives other duties typed consumers without turning the legacy debt into
# delivery.
# Test the rule BODY, left of the arrow — a plain `grep owe` matches Article 1b's
# own head and can never fail.
#
# The `:require` lines run shell commands. This case's entry in
# tests/pins/suites.json grants shell access (allow_shell), and both commands
# above run through it. Without that grant each `:require` line is a harness
# error that names the missing permission, not a failed pin.

# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE — three kinds, and only one is a verdict. A FALSE on a
# corpus name this KB never mentions is real but empty: nothing could have made
# it TRUE. A non-corpus name is not a FALSE at all — the run aborts, pins not
# trustworthy. And a well-formed query on an argument its relation never
# carries is a vacuous green that passes forever. Article 0a closed the
# ASSERTION side only — a widening fact aborts the run —
# but a QUERY on an unmentioned name still answers a clean FALSE, so kind one
# is untouched. Pin a FALSE only where the KB could have said TRUE, and say in
# the comment what would flip it.

# The environmental right and direct animal protection are exercised in
# tests/pins/ecology/: environmental-claim, domain, ceiling, high-consequence,
# residual-restoration, dual-continuity, hazard-liability, contribution-liability,
# animal-coverage, animal-ordinary-use, animal-food-*, animal-research-*,
# animal-risk-*, animal/categorical-*, upstream and counterfactual cases.
# These no-record controls become TRUE only with the respective full findings;
# the ordinary positive and withholding cases test that contrast separately.
#
# Chapter 12's "When the record the protection rested on was defective" rests
# on the ecological family's own record-lifecycle cases:
#   tests/pins/ecology/ecological-record-defect/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/ecological-record-defect/withheld/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/ecological-record-correction/positive/expect.pins.nibli
# The defect finding derives the read/stop-reliance duty, the urgent human and
# animal care duty on the independent alternate, and the audit duty, and marks
# `err(record, ECReviewedEcologicalAnimalRecordDefect)`; withheld derives all of
# them FALSE; the correction derives
# `prevents(replacement, ECCorrectionAsAutomaticRenewedAuthority)`. No stopped
# activity, continued care or restored condition follows.
#
# Chapter 13's "When a use has to be stopped" rests on the animal remedy
# orders:
#   tests/pins/ecology/animal-cessation-order/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/animal-rescue-order/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/animal-custody-order/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/animal-care-restitution-order/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/animal-use-disqualification-order/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/animal-nonrepetition-order/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/ecology/animal-human-justice/positive/expect.pins.nibli
# Each derives its own duty on the named executor. The rehoming, veterinary,
# rehabilitation, sanctuary, habitat, monitoring, structural, licence and
# record-correction orders are the same shape and have their own cases. None
# infers a performed rescue, treatment, transfer, restoration or delivery.
:expect-pins 101

# No-record controls. The environmental right and animal protection "have
# their own grounds and chapters": with no claim record for Bela and no
# coverage finding, neither the completed claim nor the animal's class as
# credibly sentient and protected follows.
? complete(ECReaderClaim, ECEnvironmentalRightClaim, Bela).
# => FALSE
? class(ECReaderAnimal, ECCrediblySentientProtectedAnimal, ECReaderCoverage).
# => FALSE

# The shell checks behind the NOTE above: the first requires that no rule body,
# left of the arrow, reads `owe`; the second requires that the same extraction
# finds bodies reading `false`, so the first cannot pass by matching nothing.
:require test -z "$(awk -F'->' '/^[^#]/ && /->/ && $1 ~ /(^|[^[:alnum:]_])owe[[:space:]]*\(/ {print}' book-1/source/constitution.nibli)"
:require test -n "$(awk -F'->' '/^[^#]/ && /->/ && $1 ~ /false/ {print}' book-1/source/constitution.nibli)"

# "The floor debt is not a receipt." The cast record lacks the evidence each
# delivery route needs, and belief and bodily safety have no delivery route at
# all, so no delivery conclusion follows for anyone asked here.
? eats(Adam).
# => FALSE

? healthy(Bela).
# => FALSE

? secure(Bela).
# => FALSE

? suffice(Bela).
# => FALSE

? learn(Cira).
# => FALSE

? believe(Bela).
# => FALSE

? meets(Hano).
# => FALSE

? dwell(Bela).
# => FALSE

# "The rules conclude that Hano is a prisoner, and Hano's shelter and recorded
# speech still wait on evidence of their own." Custody concludes no shelter:
# dwell is FALSE for Hano, and for Kel and Adam, confined with no home entry.
? dwell(Hano).
# => FALSE

? prisoner(Hano).
# => TRUE

? dwell(Kel).
# => FALSE

? dwell(Adam).
# => FALSE

# Other cast members likewise have no independently witnessed shelter receipt.
? dwell(Cira).
# => FALSE

# Custody proves no recorded speech. The ordinary expression duty remains.
? expresses(Hano).
# => FALSE

? expresses(Bela).
# => FALSE

? expresses(Jala).
# => FALSE

# The current custody and credibility graph also refuses this hostile control.
:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable/
all $x: person($x) & ~believe($x) -> false($x).

# "Other uses of a missing floor condition are held back by separate checks on
# how delivery conclusions may be used": this hostile scoped rule, recording a
# loss for lacking company, loads, which is why the development invariant bans
# all active floor-actuality readers.
:accept-scoped
all $x: person($x) & ~meets($x) -> lose(Points, $x).

# "The protection covers confinement, and it depends on how such a rule is
# written": it blocks confinement for an absence, not a rule that concludes a
# floor item, so this hostile scoped rule, concluding belief for every
# prisoner, loads.
:accept-scoped
all $x: prisoner($x) -> believe($x).

# Each `:accept-scoped` above must compile and load, that loadability is the
# pin verdict, and the statement is then retracted, so none of these controls
# widens the base and a query may be added at this point. Left resident, the
# loss rule above would fire for every person the record shows no company for,
# and every query below would run against that widened base. The `judge` and
# `capture` assertions further down are ordinary ground facts, resident from
# the point they are written, so ordering still matters for anything added
# below them.

# ── "Owed by whom" ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "The public body named State owes each floor item to every person": the
# Provision token is owed to Bela on personhood alone.
? owe(State, Provision, Bela).
# => TRUE

# scoped to persons and to nothing else: no roster entry, nothing owed
? owe(State, Provision, Sokk).
# => FALSE

# The debt is itemised beside the Provision token: each floor item is owed by
# name, and these ask some of the items for different people.
? owe(State, Eats, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Meets, Hano).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Believe, Cira).
# => TRUE

# same scoping as the token — a non-person is owed nothing, itemised or not
? owe(State, Eats, Sokk).
# => FALSE

# "Bela is owed food and shelter, and on the record as it stands the delivery
# conclusions for both are absent." Both halves, adjacent, same person: if
# either delivery conclusion flips while the entitlement stays TRUE, something
# has joined the debt to its delivery.
? entitled(Bela, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE

? eats(Bela).
# => FALSE

? dwell(Bela).
# => FALSE

# ── OWED IN FULL, ENUMERATED, ONE PERSON ─────────────────────────────────────
# "The rules conclude each of those entitlements for her, and for each item
# they name the public body that owes it" — checked on the chapter's own person
# for every item on both sides of the debt, not sampled. Only an enumeration
# checks a claim about every item, because an omitted item is exactly where
# such claims fail.
? entitled(Bela, event { secure() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Bela, event { suffice() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Bela, event { dwell() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Bela, event { healthy() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Bela, event { learn() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Bela, event { expresses() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Bela, event { believe() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Bela, event { meets() }).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Secure, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Suffice, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Dwell, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Healthy, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Learn, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Expresses, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Believe, Bela).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Meets, Bela).
# => TRUE

# "The State is itself publicly answerable".
? authority(State).
# => TRUE

# "The State's record gives it no authority to sign findings as an examiner".
# Both halves are pinned: `judge` and `capture` have no precondition, so anybody
# may record an examination of anybody, and the State records one of Bela; what
# the State lacks is the authority to sign findings that gives a recorded
# examination force.
judge(State, Bela).
capture(State, Bela).
? capture(State, Bela).
# => TRUE

? permits(Review, State).
# => FALSE

# "A rule making the absence of a protected floor condition, or of the debt
# owing it, a ground for confinement is refused before it can change anyone's
# status." The `~home` control in rights-floor.pins.nibli is what proves this
# is the obligation doing it and not the shape of the rule.
:refuse reasoning /'prisoner' -> 'owe'/
all $x: person($x) & ~owe(State, Provision, $x) -> prisoner($x).

# The same refusal on a named debt: a rule confining people for lacking the
# food debt is refused as well. Pinned because a protection extending to each
# itemised debt is the kind of claim that is assumed rather than checked.
:refuse reasoning /'prisoner' -> 'owe'/
all $x: person($x) & ~owe(State, Eats, $x) -> prisoner($x).

# The firewall reaches every item, bodily safety and material security as two:
# a rule confining someone for lacking any one of them is refused, as is one
# confining them for lacking the material-security debt.
:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~secure($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~suffice($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~eats($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~dwell($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~healthy($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~learn($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~expresses($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~believe($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~meets($x) -> prisoner($x).

:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~owe(State, Suffice, $x) -> prisoner($x).

# ── THE LEARNING ROUTE, DORMANT IN THE CAST. Ground fact persists ──────────
# Teaching that was heard concludes learning, a route separate from the
# recipient-side receipt routes. The cast record holds Bela's teaching of Cira
# and no hearing, so the route is dormant; dormant is not blind, and this pair
# is the proof. The arrival is two-sided (the hearing is written here) and it
# rates nobody: Cira learns, and the rules conclude no recognition for being
# taught.
? learn(Cira).
# => FALSE

hears(Cira, Bela).

? learn(Cira).
# => TRUE

? reward(Cira).
# => FALSE

# ── Owed by whom: the tiers ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# "The common tier finances the floor, equalises between regions, sets its
#  minimum standards and backstops it for every person; its duties need nothing
#  but personhood." Fresh constants, so no cast verdict moves.
person(Loma).
? obliged(CommonTier, FinanceEqualiseAndSetMinimumStandardsForTheFloor, Loma).
# => TRUE
? obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, Loma).
# => TRUE

# "A region must provide the floor, and a locality must reach the person and
#  deliver it, where a witness authorised for that person records the person as
#  present there."
authorized(PresenceClerk, FloorPresenceWitness, Loma).
observe(PresenceClerk, Loma, NorthRegion, FloorPresenceRegionScope).
observe(PresenceClerk, Loma, RiverTown, FloorPresenceLocalityScope).
? obliged(NorthRegion, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Loma).
# => TRUE
? obliged(RiverTown, ReachAndDeliverTheFloorLocally, Loma).
# => TRUE

# An entry by a writer nobody authorised for the person allocates nothing.
observe(Tavi, Loma, SouthRegion, FloorPresenceRegionScope).
? obliged(SouthRegion, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Loma).
# => FALSE

# A presence record allocates a duty; it is not a delivery.
? eats(Loma).
# => FALSE
? dwell(Loma).
# => FALSE

# "When a source and a separate independent reviewer, neither of them the failed
#  body, certify that a region or locality has failed, the tier they name must
#  assume continuity, and only a publicly answerable tier can be named. The
#  failed body's own duty stands."
# The tier named must be publicly answerable.
public(NorthRegion).
authorized(FloorOmbud, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, FailRiver).
authorized(FloorAuditor, IndependentFloorFailureReviewAuthority, FailRiver).
observe(FloorOmbud, FailRiver, RiverTown, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(FloorAuditor, FailRiver, RiverTown, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(FloorOmbud, FailRiver, NorthRegion, FloorContinuityTierScope).
observe(FloorAuditor, FailRiver, NorthRegion, FloorContinuityTierScope).
? obliged(NorthRegion, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, FailRiver).
# => TRUE
? obliged(RiverTown, ReachAndDeliverTheFloorLocally, Loma).
# => TRUE

# A failed body cannot certify its own failure.
authorized(RiverTown, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, FailSelf).
authorized(FloorAuditor, IndependentFloorFailureReviewAuthority, FailSelf).
observe(RiverTown, FailSelf, RiverTown, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(FloorAuditor, FailSelf, RiverTown, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(RiverTown, FailSelf, NorthRegion, FloorContinuityTierScope).
observe(FloorAuditor, FailSelf, NorthRegion, FloorContinuityTierScope).
? obliged(NorthRegion, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, FailSelf).
# => FALSE

# One attester alone certifies nothing.
authorized(FloorOmbud, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, FailLone).
observe(FloorOmbud, FailLone, RiverTown, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(FloorOmbud, FailLone, NorthRegion, FloorContinuityTierScope).
? obliged(NorthRegion, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, FailLone).
# => FALSE

# Continuity passes only to a publicly answerable tier: a certification naming a
# private provider obliges it to nothing.
authorized(FloorOmbud, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, FailToProvider).
authorized(FloorAuditor, IndependentFloorFailureReviewAuthority, FailToProvider).
observe(FloorOmbud, FailToProvider, RiverTown, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(FloorAuditor, FailToProvider, RiverTown, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(FloorOmbud, FailToProvider, RiverFoodContractor, FloorContinuityTierScope).
observe(FloorAuditor, FailToProvider, RiverFoodContractor, FloorContinuityTierScope).
? obliged(RiverFoodContractor, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, FailToProvider).
# => FALSE

# "None of these allocations is a condition of the floor." A rule confining a
# person for lacking the common tier's duty is refused exactly as one confining
# them for lacking the debt. The engine names whichever edge of the resulting
# cycle it meets first, so the pin matches the stratification refusal itself;
# the `~home` control in rights-floor.pins.nibli shows that a rule reading
# something outside the person cone still loads.
:refuse reasoning /Unstratifiable negation: strongly-connected component containing/
all $x: person($x) & ~obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, $x) -> prisoner($x).

# ── The child with nobody ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "Every person is owed the same list." The pins ask every debt and every
# entitlement of the child by name rather than sampling, because the claim is
# that the list does not shorten for anybody.
? owe(State, Eats, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Dwell, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Healthy, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Learn, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Secure, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Suffice, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Expresses, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Believe, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Meets, Nell).
# => TRUE

# The tiers reach the child without any record beyond the birth entry: the
# common tier's duties follow, and no region owes provision on a presence nobody
# recorded.
? obliged(CommonTier, FinanceEqualiseAndSetMinimumStandardsForTheFloor, Nell).
# => TRUE
? obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, Nell).
# => TRUE
? obliged(NorthRegion, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Nell).
# => FALSE

# "Each entitlement follows from personhood alone": the birth entry makes the
# child a person, and every floor entitlement follows, one query per item.
? entitled(Nell, event { eats() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { dwell() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { healthy() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { learn() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { secure() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { suffice() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { expresses() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { believe() }).
# => TRUE

? entitled(Nell, event { meets() }).
# => TRUE

# Nothing is asked of the child, and nothing follows against the child: the
# birth entry concludes no custody.
? prisoner(Nell).
# => FALSE
